1
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and let
it fly until it's gone.

3
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:29,360
Joking around with the gym teacher Kashiwa,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for
staying so full of energy.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
Seriously, I'm only sure of this.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,020
One nightmare, and nothing changes.

8
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,880
The streets feel even kinder.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,900
it's already getting dark.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,820
Are you going to look at the yakitori stall?

12
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:59,240
From the pointed hat's books,

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,060
the sunset falls toward the earth.

14
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too,
it'll end with the sun going down.

15
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,720
I wonder if happiness will come again.

16
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,660
I took the easy way and realized it.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool.

18
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:26,980
Chief, please just stay in bed.

19
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:57,340
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

20
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:57,640
Aaagh!

21
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:58,980
Noooo!

22
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,926
Because you went and polished the windows
spotless first thing in the morning,

23
00:02:02,976 --> 00:02:04,380
look what's happened to me!

24
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,600
Ryo-chan, you're disgusting!

25
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:08,080
Ugh, what a mess!

26
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:08,940
Ryo-san!

27
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:15,060
Hey! I'm not a dog!

28
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:16,720
Well, how cold.

29
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:21,320
Because an important guest is coming today,

30
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:23,580
we were told to be extra
careful not to make any blunders.

31
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:26,860
Chief Ohara gave us a stern warning.

32
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,840
So what about me, then?

33
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,020
Talk of an important guest coming,

34
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:34,220
as a senior constable,
I haven't done anything wrong.

35
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:37,980
they said that if they told Ryo-san,
it would turn into a mess.

36
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:40,880
Chief Ohara must have been worried, too.

37
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:44,900
An inspector from the National
Police Agency is coming today, senpai.

38
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:45,860
Inspection.

39
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:49,420
They're grading the performance
reports of police boxes nationwide.

40
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,420
Bye-bye.

41
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:57,560
Also known as the Police Box Michelin.

42
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,880
It's like a ranking chart for police boxes.

43
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,960
You've heard of it, Ryo-chan, right?

44
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,660
Now that you mention it...

45
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:09,260
every five years, surprise inspections
hit police boxes all across the country.

46
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:10,460
Hey, wait a minute!

47
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,340
This way,
it's obvious we knew they were coming!

48
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,540
It's just like a school home visit.

49
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,980
Anyway,
if we make it into the top three teams,

50
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,280
we get the honor of being a model police box,
plus a cash prize.

51
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:25,580
A cash prize?

52
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,100
Heh heh heh.

53
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:32,880
Bye-bye!

54
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,547
Forget the prize money,

55
00:03:36,597 --> 00:03:40,092
a top-three finish is a
lifelong wish for Chief Ohara.

56
00:03:40,142 --> 00:03:42,160
We want to help too!

57
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:50,140
I believe a police box should be a reliable shield
protecting the safety and peace of mind of citizens' daily lives,

58
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:55,820
and I hope the inspectors will see the daily efforts of you all,
who share this same goal,

59
00:03:55,820 --> 00:04:00,940
and that police officers across the nation will come to know of them.
I truly, truly hope so.

60
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:03,220
The chief said such a thing...

61
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:07,600
That's why Ryo-chan especially has to behave himself,
or we're in trouble.

62
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,747
Don't make fun of me!

63
00:04:08,797 --> 00:04:12,240
I'm not a kid!
When it counts, I get it done!

64
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,840
So, where's the chief? He's still not here?

65
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:19,400
He said he'd show up early today,
but now that you mention it, he's late.

66
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,040
He's here.

67
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,800
You're late, Chief!

68
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:36,300
Sorry, sorry, sorry, Terai.

69
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,880
Wait, Ryotsu.

70
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,440
Yeah.

71
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:42,620
Preparations are complete, Chief Ohara.

72
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,340
I see, Reiko.

73
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:47,420
Come on, Reiko's a young lady, Chief.

74
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,200
Good work, Reiko.

75
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:53,420
Everyone helped out too.

76
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,300
I see, I see.

77
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,130
Ah

78
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:01,000
Uh ah

79
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,140
It's Terai.

80
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:04,360
Right, it's Officer Terai.

81
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:07,320
Chief.

82
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,440
Nakagawa, it's Nakagawa.

83
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:11,660
Thanks for your work, Nakagawa.

84
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,840
Why are you getting nervous already?

85
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:17,140
Pull yourself together, Chief!

86
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,271
Ah ah...

87
00:05:19,321 --> 00:05:22,320
Ah ah ah...

88
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:24,160
Huh?

89
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,900
Everything's spinning...

90
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,140
Chief!

91
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,380
Are you all right, Chief?

92
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:35,100
Pull yourself together!

93
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,740
Honestly, Ryo-chan, you're so rough!

94
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,640
I was only lightly...

95
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:42,900
What? I just tripped a little!

96
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:48,900
Speaking of which, I completely forgot I
had an important announcement for everyone!

97
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,360
Something's stuck to you, Ryotsu.

98
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:58,340
Didn't you wash your face?
What a hopeless guy.

99
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:01,820
Hey, are your eyebrows joined together?

100
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:06,020
"Huh" isn't the point, Chief.

101
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:08,160
Chief, he's acting strange, isn't he?

102
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,920
Yeah, quite a lot.

103
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,500
I wonder what's wrong with him.

104
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,480
Chief.

105
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,760
What's wrong?

106
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:15,740
Chief.

107
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,480
Wow, you've got a fever, Chief!

108
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,000
I'm fine.

109
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,760
Don't mind me, just keep up your duties.

110
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,560
Chief, you should lie down.

111
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,480
Yeah, you should.

112
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:33,460
Really, I'm fine, so don't worry about it.

113
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,380
Chief.

114
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:35,720
Yaa.

115
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,660
This is bad.

116
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,420
What was it that works for fevers?

117
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,460
Nakagawa, lend me a shoulder.

118
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:43,080
Yes.

119
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:45,120
Eiko, bring a futon to the back room.

120
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,280
I'll go buy some daikon!

121
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:51,560
Hey! Why is he going out to buy daikon right now,
that guy!

122
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:54,660
So, a pot? You need a pot, right?

123
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:58,275
No! A futon,

124
00:06:58,325 --> 00:06:59,940
Reiko!

125
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:00,820
Yes!

126
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,646
Sorry about this.

127
00:07:04,696 --> 00:07:09,300
We have medicine, so if he stays
like this for a while, he'll be fine.

128
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:15,260
Shouldn't we have him rest here for a while,
and once he calms down, send him home?

129
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,040
Right.

130
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:19,880
With someone this seriously ill...

131
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:23,660
I can't understand what you're saying anymore,
so you don't need to talk, Chief.

132
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:29,640
When the inspectors arrive,
I'll greet them, so be sure to wake me up.

133
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:34,940
Chief!

134
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,760
Boo, boo!

135
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,280
Aaaaaah!

136
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,880
Lying there in such a confusing way!

137
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:55,340
Fine. Terai has gone out to buy the medicine,
so the three of us have to get through this crisis.

138
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,520
Yes, sorry.

139
00:07:58,140 --> 00:07:59,100
They're here!

140
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,080
Thanks as always.

141
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,980
Today was the delivery date.

142
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:07,020
What is this Araka Plastic thing?

143
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:12,520
It's the Robo Deka Banchou
figure I had the factory make.

144
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:19,040
Robo Deka Banchou is a character from the manga the
senior officer was serializing as a side job, right?

145
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,860
Never mind that,
have them bring over the food with a smile.

146
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:24,820
The factory's delivery was a week late,

147
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:29,680
and if I don't paint it and ship it to the customer today,
there'll be trouble.

148
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:35,380
Me, of all people, completely forgetting
something this important until now!

149
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:36,320
Oof.

150
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,160
You're not planning to start painting here,
are you?

151
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:44,220
Don't worry, I'll knock it out
quickly before the inspectors arrive.

152
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,540
There's no way you can finish
painting this in an hour or two.

153
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:50,000
The inspectors are going to show up, senior!

154
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,920
Whether it's finished or not,
I've got to paint it before they get here.

155
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:58,220
Now I'm getting dizzy too.
I'll go check on the Chief.

156
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:00,900
Nakagawa.

157
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:03,360
Look at this.

158
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,200
What's wrong with the homepage?

159
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,000
The problem is right here.

160
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,720
Why is my photo on it!

161
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:18,600
Thanks to that, orders for the Robo Teka
Punch Ofijia poured in at ten times the target.

162
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:21,120
This is a violation of portrait rights!

163
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,960
Doing something like
this without permission...

164
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,300
It won't come off, it won't come off.

165
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:28,600
So if the figure shipment is delayed,

166
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,960
you'll be in trouble too, won't you?

167
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,360
That's not fair, senpai.

168
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,960
Give up, Nakagawa.

169
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,140
We're in this together.

170
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:42,260
Fine, I get it.

171
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,680
I guess I'll just help, then.

172
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,720
I'll help.

173
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,660
Then we need to hide this somewhere, quick.

174
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,460
Good, that's a good attitude.

175
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,580
Paint it so it doesn't go outside the lines.

176
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,540
Every single one is going up for sale,
so be careful.

177
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:03,480
I know.

178
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,220
See, it's sticking out. You're clumsy.

179
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,140
Reiko-kun.

180
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,000
Yes?

181
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,280
What's sticking out?

182
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:12,040
Chief.

183
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:14,620
If the Chief wakes up and finds out,
we'll be in trouble.

184
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:18,480
Ryo-chan, you're all being too loud.

185
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:22,620
Hey, what's sticking out?

186
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:26,460
I heard you've come
down with a fever, Chief.

187
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:33,160
My legs have gone numb from sitting seiza,
like a zodiac sign that can't be a bonus.

188
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,440
Please bear with it that much.

189
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,580
My situation is even worse, after all.

190
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:42,500
This guy casually bragged about having long legs,
didn't he?

191
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,140
N-no, that's not it!

192
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:46,940
What's not it, Reiko?

193
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,240
No, Chief.

194
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:51,580
Whose legs are long, Reiko?

195
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:54,660
See, they can hear
everything from over there!

196
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:58,200
What can they hear, Reiko?

197
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:58,760
That's...

198
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,980
It's the senior's fault, isn't it?

199
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:04,220
Which senior is to blame, Nakagawa?

200
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:05,900
I'll do this to you two too.

201
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,080
What are you going to do?

202
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:10,200
Hey, hey, hey!

203
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:10,600
Hey, come on!

204
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,940
Aaaaah!

205
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,220
Reiko!

206
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:17,660
What are we supposed to do with this?!
I'm not taking the blame!

207
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,120
Reiko!

208
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,820
Yes, yes, Chief.

209
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:24,220
Shouldn't the inspectors be arriving soon?

210
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,760
Ugh, no, Chief.

211
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,540
You still need to lie down and rest.

212
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:29,660
When they arrive, I'll wake you properly.

213
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,560
I see. Sorry, Reiko.

214
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:34,180
You're welcome, Chief.

215
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:37,640
I wonder if we can get
through today like this.

216
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,380
This place is a punishment too.

217
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:50,000
But everything everywhere is a mess.

218
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,200
It's nothing but police boxes.

219
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,800
Where to next?

220
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,580
Take me to Kameari.

221
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,300
What's wrong?

222
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,620
You came?

223
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:26,940
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh...

224
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,960
Did you do this, Terai!

225
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,080
Is it a fever or what?!

226
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,758
Hot! If you keep collecting stuff like that,

227
00:12:33,808 --> 00:12:37,020
that Kisoshu-san gets
introduced all the time, so...

228
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:39,140
The doctor's house call should come first!

229
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,060
Well, it's tiny...

230
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,280
It was a crime!

231
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:46,840
Hey! I'm not the sick one!

232
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:47,720
What?

233
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,020
Then...

234
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:50,340
I made it across!

235
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,920
No, it isn't!

236
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,920
That was close.

237
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,400
I hope the chief's fever goes down.

238
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,920
I'm sure it'll go up, for sure.

239
00:13:15,780 --> 00:13:18,600
It looks like the cleaning
is thorough at first glance,

240
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,920
but it's actually a makeshift cover-up job.

241
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:23,100
An obvious punishment.

242
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:37,380
I'm Senior Constable Ryotsu.

243
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,780
Introductions aren't necessary.

244
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:41,940
Please continue your duties as usual.

245
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:44,420
We'll conduct our inspection on our own.

246
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:47,420
We'll call you over when we need you.

247
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:47,920
Yes.

248
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:51,040
As expected, you're sharp.

249
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,700
The grading's strict too.

250
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,280
But it comes off as snide.

251
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:56,480
But the real problem starts here.

252
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,320
Help me!

253
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,740
I'm being eaten alive!

254
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:03,780
Aaah!

255
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,560
Chichin puripin yoo!

256
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,740
Puuu~

257
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:07,300
Phew~

258
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,480
What on earth is that
voice coming from the back?

259
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,500
Someone give us a proper explanation.

260
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,320
Yo!

261
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:16,360
Emergency drill, begin!

262
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,660
Hey, wait! Drop your weapons!

263
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:22,040
You guys, shout something too!

264
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,080
Let go of my arm!

265
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,980
Your mom's gonna be heartbroken, you know.

266
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:28,080
How's that?

267
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,180
But this guy's...

268
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:35,980
That's how all of us here at the station stay on edge every day,
never slacking off on our training,

269
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:38,180
always ready for an emergency.

270
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:40,960
Drill

271
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,242
Yes, notice item number one,

272
00:14:43,292 --> 00:14:45,200
emergency drill suddenly initiated.

273
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:49,020
Don't bite, don't bite there. Stop it!

274
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,860
So, who's in the back?

275
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,500
He escaped, he escaped, he escaped!

276
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,760
Help me!

277
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,680
Who's in there?

278
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:01,740
The Battle of the Sweltering Town

279
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,220
That's a recording tape.

280
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:06,060
Tape.

281
00:15:06,060 --> 00:15:09,380
Hey, you in that car!
This is a no standing or parking zone!

282
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,260
Aaaaaaah!

283
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:26,580
See, it stopped, because it's just tape, it's tape!
Neither a good nor a bad rating, but thanks to you, senpai, we seem to have gotten through the worst of it.

284
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:31,040
Right, then I'd like to hear
from the person in charge.

285
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:37,920
Hey, are you the person in charge? Please call Sergeant Daijiro Ohara,
the section chief.

286
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,240
What do we do?

287
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,600
The section chief is right now...

288
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:44,380
I see, so the section chief is absent?

289
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:45,440
Punishment.

290
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,780
Wait, Chief Ohara is here.

291
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:49,900
Reiko-san.

292
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:50,780
But...

293
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:53,460
Then please call him, right now.

294
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,080
He's here, but...

295
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,140
He's here, but he can't show his face.

296
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:58,480
So that's how it is.

297
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:02,060
So the section chief is arrogant,
lazy, and eccentric, is he?

298
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:02,980
Punishment.

299
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:03,960
No, that's not it.

300
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,180
Reiko-san.

301
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,640
Please don't write that down.

302
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:10,340
Obstruction of official duties.

303
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,040
Your guidance and training are also lacking.

304
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:15,580
Senior Officer Daijirō Ōhara.

305
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:17,980
As squad leader, you're irresponsible.

306
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,080
That's a penalty.

307
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:24,680
What do you think you're doing?

308
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,760
Penalty, penalty,
you've been saying that since earlier.

309
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:29,460
What do you think I am, anyway?

310
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:31,920
I've received orders
from the police station,

311
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,500
and I'm only here to inspect.

312
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,500
Give it back.

313
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:39,160
No way. You're trying to discipline Reiko-san.
You picked the wrong opponent, Reiko-san.

314
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:47,860
Which side are you two on? Tsuke is so cheeky, and on top of that, Batsu...
My name is Reiko Akimoto. Did you return it properly here?

315
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:58,780
I'll go get the Chief now,
so please wait right there.

316
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,400
Ryo-chan, Ryo-chan, it's a disaster!

317
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,200
This is the bigger disaster!

318
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:08,500
The inspector says he wants to see the Chief!
What do we do, Ryo-chan?

319
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:11,280
What do you mean,
"what do we do"? There's nothing we can do about this!

320
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,820
I already said I'd go get him!

321
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:15,860
Why would you go and
say something like that?

322
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:19,620
If you don't need people, then give me back!

323
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:20,960
Not now!

324
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,540
Don't come to me asking what to do!

325
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,120
I'd rather you help me with this!

326
00:17:28,940 --> 00:17:30,960
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

327
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:33,700
Sorry to keep you waiting.
This is Chief Ohara.

328
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:35,920
Chief.

329
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:41,900
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I'm Daijiro Ohara, the team leader.

330
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:47,560
Ryo-chan,
a handshake is out of the question.

331
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:53,120
What can I do for you?

332
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:58,080
Then let me ask you a few quick questions.

333
00:17:58,780 --> 00:17:59,380
Anything at all.

334
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:02,880
Ryo-chan, we're working hard for the Chief.

335
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:06,940
Just as I thought, if we stop now,
we'll be counting on you, senpai.

336
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:08,120
Very well.

337
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:10,940
So what kind of police
box are you aiming for?

338
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:12,740
Please answer briefly.

339
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:14,760
Within five seconds.

340
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:15,960
One second.

341
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,020
Two seconds.

342
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:17,040
Three seconds.

343
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:18,620
Well, that would be...

344
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:20,500
It's a comfortable police box.

345
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:24,840
Define comfort concretely,
within three seconds.

346
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:25,720
One second.

347
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:29,020
Well, in other words,
we improve the treatment of the officers,

348
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:32,640
and by aiming for a police box where
we can work happily and comfortably,

349
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,260
everyone's morale will rise,

350
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:36,122
and in turn, the safety of citizens' lives,

351
00:18:36,172 --> 00:18:39,200
and a peaceful life will follow.
That's the idea.

352
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,940
In other words,
considering the times we live in,

353
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:45,920
it's desirable from now on to have one computer per person,
don't you think.

354
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,880
The break room has bunk beds.

355
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:51,800
Since on night shifts, it's a hassle to
lay out and fold up futons every time,

356
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,880
and if we leave them laid out,
Reiko scolds us.

357
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,220
Oh-chan.

358
00:18:56,860 --> 00:18:58,900
Looks like he's getting carried away.

359
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:03,860
A Digital Sun plasma TV,

360
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:05,640
super thin and large,

361
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:07,800
since that break room is so cramped.

362
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,900
Plasma?

363
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,440
And of course, a bath, I guess.

364
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,960
The kind with bubbles.

365
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:14,880
And a sauna too, if possible.

366
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:18,000
Plus a private mountain bike.

367
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:21,680
Uh-oh.

368
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:22,520
We'll get caught!

369
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,300
Fish!

370
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,240
There he goes again.

371
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:29,640
Is that man the team leader here?

372
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:30,860
Well, yes, sort of.

373
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:35,680
What is it?

374
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,620
Right away, I'll get some tea

375
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:42,060
Honestly, Ryo-chan

376
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:45,060
Phew, huff, huff

377
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,220
Are you all right, Chief?

378
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:49,900
What a disaster

379
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:53,620
My Robozega Banchou has
turned all old-hag-looking

380
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:55,620
How did it come to this?

381
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:57,960
At this rate, they look like
jizo statues and Buddha images

382
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:58,780
Temple-y

383
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,280
Brings back memories

384
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:04,120
We used to do this a lot
as side jobs back in the day

385
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,560
Painting colors like this

386
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:08,120
Hey, don't go choosing colors on your own!

387
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:11,420
I explained earlier that there's a set color scheme,
didn't I?

388
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:12,440
Did I?

389
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,260
It's just that I couldn't find a sample

390
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:21,580
I tried it, but everything came out wrong!

391
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:32,100
You said this part is black, so that's the face, and now you're the berserker!
Talking to someone who's helping all of us like that, you're the one who'll end up in trouble.

392
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,240
Mr. Ryotsu

393
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:43,440
Please, listen carefully. From here to here is the hair,
and the Logan, but I can't see the boundary very well.

394
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:46,120
No, I said you can't
make it all pitch black.

395
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:49,620
Don't leave me alone like this!

396
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:51,680
The inspection isn't over yet.

397
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:55,680
The fever that was coming
down has gone back up.

398
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:59,460
The inspector says he wants
to see Chief Ohara again.

399
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:01,020
What do we do, Ryo-chan?

400
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,820
What should we do?

401
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,540
If it comes to this, I'll go.

402
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:16,220
Do you still have something to ask me?

403
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:16,700
Yes.

404
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,800
W-who are you?

405
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,020
Where's Kankichi Ryotsu?

406
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:28,360
R-Ryotsu... K-Kankichi...

407
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,280
Where's Ryotsu?

408
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,840
Ryotsu, Ryotsu!

409
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,880
Spy, help!

410
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,160
Senpai!

411
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:38,720
W-what are you talking about?

412
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:41,380
It's me, Chief Ohara, Ryotsu.

413
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:43,220
What a madman!

414
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:45,420
There he is, it's Ryotsu!

415
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,580
Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

416
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:50,800
We have to tell him the delivery is late!

417
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:53,480
The figures! The figures! The figures!

418
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,560
Hand over the figures!

419
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,120
The delivery date?

420
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,080
The figures?

421
00:21:58,620 --> 00:21:59,540
Give back the money!

422
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:02,040
The figures!

423
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:04,240
This is bad!

424
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:09,600
What color was this part again, Ryo-san?

425
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:14,800
Wigira! Wigira! Wigira! Wigira!

426
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,020
You can't go out dressed like that!

427
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:16,960
Whoa!

428
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:17,760
Aaah -

429
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:21,800
a shield that protects the safety
and peace of mind of everyday life

430
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:26,800
I believe we must be a reassuring shield.

431
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:30,080
And you gentlemen who share this sentiment,

432
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:30,800
This guy has broken the bond!

433
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:34,300
we absolutely want the
inspector to see our efforts

434
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:38,060
and want police officers across
the country to know about them,

435
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:41,140
I strongly believe.

436
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:50,180
Rain or shine, wind or snow, it's because
Katsushika Ward has the Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

437
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:53,280
In other words, let me explain this to you.

438
00:22:57,540 --> 00:23:01,840
Batter! Bat! Bat! Bat! Bat! Bat! Bat! Bat!

439
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:03,320
Rainbow!

440
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:11,280
Aaaaaaah!

441
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:17,600
Five officers from the Kameari Kōen-mae police box are being transferred to Hyōzan,
apparently.

442
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:27,700
What are we supposed to do here?
Rain or shine, wind or snow,

443
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:32,280
it's fine, because Katsushika Ward
has the Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

444
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:38,760
we want people to think how lucky they are
that the Kameari Kōen-mae police box exists.

445
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:52,960
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out

446
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:59,540
I walked looking back,
tugged along by the gacha

447
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:06,780
That strange feeling I had back then

448
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:11,960
So, on the tiles of the arcade street

449
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:17,740
I tried walking only on the black ones

450
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:25,900
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets

451
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:33,340
Even the smug-faced politicians
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

452
00:24:33,860 --> 00:24:38,920
Go on, turn that corner

453
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:44,120
You can meet everyone, everyone

454
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:48,740
Over there, there's a turtle

455
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:52,100
Surely there's a turtle

456
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:57,380
Everyone, come on over to our town

457
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:01,980
Over there, there's a turtle,

458
00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:05,240
surely there's a turtle.

459
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:10,440
Everyone, come to our town!

460
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:12,080
Thank you!

461
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:17,720
Reiko has brought a super-rich prince here.

462
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:21,060
If he likes us,
we should get a fantastic reward.

463
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:24,100
What, you want to go sightseeing in Tokyo?

464
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:25,920
Then leave it to me.

465
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:28,860
I'll make memories you'll never
forget for the rest of your life.

466
00:25:29,300 --> 00:25:32,740
Next time,
take good care of Reiko's cute prince, okay?

467
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:35,700
Over there, there's a turtle,

468
00:25:36,980 --> 00:25:39,040
well, surely there's a turtle.

469
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:44,220
Everyone, come to our town!

470
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:45,800
Thank you!

